# Copy to wazuh-docker/.env (git-ignored) after cloning upstream and applying these overrides.
#
# INDEXER_PASSWORD and DASHBOARD_PASSWORD must match whatever bcrypt hashes are actually loaded
# into the live security index - changing this file alone does nothing on its own. See
# ../README.md "Credentials" for how to rotate them (hash.sh + securityadmin.sh) and why.
#
# If you have NOT rotated internal_users.yml, use the upstream demo values (public - this is the
# well-known wazuh-docker quickstart default, not a secret):
#   INDEXER_PASSWORD=SecretPassword
#   DASHBOARD_PASSWORD=kibanaserver
# If you HAVE rotated them (recommended - see the README), put your own chosen passwords here
# instead, matching the hashes you generated. Never commit the real values in this file.
INDEXER_PASSWORD=<set after rotating, or SecretPassword if using the upstream demo hash>
DASHBOARD_PASSWORD=<set after rotating, or kibanaserver if using the upstream demo hash>
API_PASSWORD=<choose your own - no hash-file dependency, the manager sets this at startup>
